A||||6||GT Bastard||anyone checked their timing?||||1
Z||000000||GT Bastard||10-09-1999||10:48 PM||||I'm trying to check my Fiero's engine timing and i can't even see the timing marks!  has anyone else timed their Fiero's?  How did you manage to do it?  thanks....||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||10-09-1999||11:06 PM||||Jumper pins A and B of the ALDL connector to force the timing to lock at 10 degrees. Then check the timing.<P>The timing is also used for idle control (smoothing) so it is normal for it to jump all over hell when not in ALDL mode. Some engines are pretty solid at idle though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||10-10-1999||01:10 AM||||I know how to jumper to two connectors, but how do you even see the timing marks?||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-10-1999||02:24 AM||||Paint the mark on the harmonic balancer with White-Out or some of your wifes day-glo finger nail polish.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||10-10-1999||02:31 AM||||Just did mine today, since I rebuilt the distributor and had mine timing light was previously on the fritz.  I thought I was pretty close but I was at about 16 degrees BTC instead of 10.  Fixed it and now I can hardly hear the exhaust leak, and I can really tell the difference in response.<P>For the V6 you have to shine the light straight down just to the rear of the thermostat housing. <P>I am assuming that you have the timing light magnetic pickup connected to the #1 plug wire.  Otherwise, the mark will not be in the right place when th elight triggers.||||reg||12
Z||000005||GT Bastard||10-10-1999||01:50 PM||||Thanks fella's, that's all I needed to know. I'm gonna give it a try tomorrow I think. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||dogtired||10-12-1999||05:41 AM||||White-out works great. I had to go in through the wheel well to paint mine? Couldn't get my fat hand straight down, especially while trying to hold that little brush. Thats on my V6, I never did it on a 4. Good Luck.||||reg||6
